A={
('rasharkin-directory-1912','thomas-ross'):('The original 1901 Gortereghy return describes Thomas Ross, 34, as farmer and flax miller, with Scotland-born wife Mary Jane and children. This strongly supports the 1912 mill-owner occurrence. The 1911 household reports 24 years of marriage. Ross-13124 remains compatible, with differing reported census ages. Ross-29596 has severe chronology tension if his cited 1874 birth is correct: he would be about 12 at marriage and 11 when Jeannie was born. The birth image returned HTTP403, so this remains a conditional conflict rather than a fresh original-based exclusion. Ross-25888 has a separate Gransha/Ann Jane family; Ross-29600 is Robert T Ross, who died in 1909.','Inspect the original Thomas/Mary Jane marriage and Ross-29596 birth image to identify Thomas’s father and settle the candidate chronology.'),
('rasharkin-directory-1912','peter-mccaughern'):('The original 1911 Dreen return names Peter McCaughern, 48, single Roman Catholic farmer, and his sister Agnes, 55. This is a concrete family comparison for the 1912 grocer/farmer and later Dreen probates. Directory-to-census continuity remains probable; the probate original was not inspected. Searches for McCaughern, McCaughan, McCarnagh and McCahern identified no supported profile. No father is evidenced.','Inspect the 1916 Dreen probate and death entry against the 1911 household; William the administrator is not thereby proved a father or brother.'),
('rasharkin-directory-1912','robert-mccaughern'):('The original 1911 Lisnagaver return names Robert McCaughern, 54, farmer, and wife Mary Anne, 58, married 28 years. This strongly identifies the 1912 directory farmer. McCaughan-13 remains an unplaced, undated name-only lead, without an exclusion based on missing fields. Exact McCaughern, McCarnagh and McCahern searches returned zero. Mary Anne may be compared with McCaughern-24, but age and name alone neither identify nor exclude her.','Find the original marriage about 1883 using Robert/Mary Anne and surname variants; inspect parent clauses before extending the Sarah Dysart family.'),
('rasharkin-directory-1912','john-wallace'):('The original 1911 Lisnagaver teacher is Derry-born John Wallace, 55, with Antrim-born wife Mary Anne, 52, married 26 years, and six resident children. This strongly identifies the 1912 directory teacher. Wallace-17947 and Wallace-3457 remain weak candidates; unsupported birthplace fields are not sole exclusions. Wallace-26687 is excluded as a living 1911 teacher because his cited death entry records a single student who died in 1880. That candidate death original was not freshly inspected.','Inspect the teacher’s original marriage and candidate life records using wife Mary Anne and children Mary H, William G, James G, Samuel G, Sarah G and Letitia C.'),
('prescott-rochester-james-family','alexander-glasco'):('The previously inspected C114 deed explicitly identifies Alexander Glasco, Rochester express agent, as son of James formerly of Prescott, carpenter. Glasgow-951 remains a qualified candidate; Irish property occupancy does not prove physical presence in 1868. A newly inspected Rochester index card supplies an Alexander Glasgow death lead in the Union and Advertiser of 29 August 1892, page 5 column 6. It gives no age, occupation or parent, so it cannot yet identify the express agent or exclude Glasgow-951, who died in 1888.','Read the 29 August 1892 newspaper article and compare US/Canadian census records, occupation and father James before identifying the express agent with Glasgow-951.'),
('prescott-rochester-james-family','james-glasgow'):('Previously inspected deeds B395, B601 and C114 consolidate three expressly named children of one James, formerly Prescott carpenter: Eliza Jane, Mary and Alexander the express agent. Robert Glasgow-4150’s brother James remains a property-based hypothesis, without proved profile identity. Preserve one family draft and the direct father clauses; fractions do not establish a complete child count. The complete Glasgow/Glasco searches identified no supported carpenter profile. Glasgow-3743 remains an unplaced lead rather than an exclusion based solely on geography.','Read Rochester James death notices of January 1893 and Prescott/Rochester censuses to identify this carpenter and his siblings.'),
('rasharkin-john-elder-marriages','john-elder'):('This queue is partly matched. Elder-5907 matches the original 12 May 1886 John Elder/Annie Patterson marriage. The 1912 grocer/postmaster remains compatible with Elder-5907. The distinct 1842 John/Peggy marriage remains unresolved, with older Elder-7230 and Elder-4387 as weak candidates. No source proves the 1842 groom to be Elder-5907’s father. The 1886 register explicitly names father John Elder, farmer; that father’s profile identity is unknown.','Inspect the original 1842 marriage and records identifying the 1886 father John. Preserve all three finding-specific dispositions.'),
('gortereghy-elder-households-1911','william-elder'):('The original 1911 return proves William, 40, and Elizabeth, 50, a sibling pair. Elder-3951 and Elder-3950 remain compatible together. The original 1901 James/Mary household records William as 23 and Lizzie as 25. These substantial age differences are visible in the originals and must not be forced into agreement. James Elder-3946 and Mary Jane remain qualified parent identities for the 1901 children; continuity with the 1911 pair remains uncertain.','Inspect original births, family Bible entries and death/probate records to resolve the 1901/1911 age conflicts.'),
('gortereghy-elder-households-1911','elizabeth-elder'):('The original 1911 return proves Elizabeth, 50, sister of William, 40. Elder-3950 and Elder-3951 remain compatible together. Original 1901 Lizzie is 25, daughter of James, 80, and Mary, 73; William is 23. These are substantial original-record age conflicts. Retain the shared parent hypothesis at its uncertainty; do not attach the 1911 pair certainly to James Elder-3946 through these records alone.','Inspect original births and family Bible entries, preserving the conflicting original ages until resolved.')}
